HTML DOM

Document Object Model
.structured representation of a web page 
.allows developers to access, modify, and control webpage content and structure using JS
.it powers most dynamic website interactions, enabling features like real-time updates, form validation, and interactive user interfaces 
.its a tree structure 
    .each HTML tag is a node 
    .<html> is the root element 
        .contains both <head> and <body> as child elements
.container elements - those nesting other elements 
.child elements - don't contain other elements 
.the hierarchy allows developers to navigate and manipulate web page content using JS 
    .by traversing from parent to child and vice versa 

Structure 
    .document  ==  root 
    .HTML tags == branches 
    .attributes, texts and other elements == leaves 


Requirement/ Need for DOM
.dynamic content updates 
    .allows content updates without reloading the page e.g form validation
.user interaction 
    .it makes the webpage interactive e.g responding to button clicks
.flexibility  
    .devs can add, modify, or remove elements and styles in real time 
.cross-platform compatibility 
    .provides standard way for scripts to interact with web documents, ensuring browser compatibility

Working of DOM
.it connects the webpage to JS, allowing me to:
    .access elements 
    .modify content 
    .react to event 
    .create or remove elements dynamically 

Types of DOM
.3 parts:
    .Core DOM
        .standard model for all document types 
    .XML DOM 
        .standard model for XML documents 
    .HTML DOM 
        .standard model for HTML documents     

